## Step 5 — do not move these

- **Terms + curriculum links stay at the bottom**, below the next-steps dropdown. CJ
  explicitly does not want them near the top.
- **Next steps is a collapsed `<details>` directly under the payment buttons.** Green
  outline/background so it is easy to spot. Summary subline: **"Self enroll or a 5
  minute call with CJ — pick your path."** Inside: **two path tabs** — **Self Enroll**
  (3 onboarding steps) and **5 Minute Call with CJ** (call/text CJ to walk through
  welcome email, login, Mark kickoff, Mastermind). Never imply self-enroll is the only
  option. Closed by default, always openable, never gated on payment. First open fires
  `next_steps_opened`. Path taps fire `next_path_self` or `next_path_cj`. Do not hide
  this section until checkout.
- **Post-pay copy is ONE welcome email only.** Never say two emails, a second login
  email, or waiting for credentials. Step 1: welcome email → **Sales Training Login Link
  (Bookmark this)** → create password → start modules → bookmark/save email. Step 2:
  book kickoff with Mark. Step 3: join Mastermind. Canonical login URL:
  `https://members.highticketsalesacademy.com/users/sign_in`
- **Enrollment pages are enrollment only.** Do **not** add All HTSA Resources, proof
  squares, Trustpilot blocks, or CJ Reviews. Proof and resources belong on **pre-call**
  pages (`r/<slug>/`), not close pages.
- **Terms acceptance happens after plan selection**, inside the confirm sheet. Never
  gate the payment buttons behind a terms checkbox again. That is what killed
  conversion on the legacy page.
- **The guarantee stays navy and green.** No gold, no brown, no yellow.
- **No curriculum content on the page itself.** Outcomes in the "What you're getting"
  list, detail behind the modal. A visible module list invites evaluation at the
  moment CJ needs a decision.

## Step 6 — verify before reporting done

1. Page height under 3,500px at 390px width.
2. No horizontal scroll at 320px and 375px. No console errors.
3. No rendered text under 12px.
4. Header shows Prepared for (their name/email/phone) and Prepared by (CJ).
5. Only the options in `show` are present, in that order.
6. Footer business card renders with the headshot.
7. Tapping a plan opens the confirm sheet. Continue stays disabled until the box is
   checked. On continue, `recordTermsAgreement` fires before the redirect.
8. In reactivation mode: 3-pay goes to `plan_YrqGOXMxGbOVa` (true 3-pay, no
   fourth-payment warning). ClarityPay goes to `plan_VUSDju20gTBCg` ($6k), not
   the $7,200 closer plan.
9. If Splitit was requested: `"splitit"` is in `show`, card/popup say **$600/mo ·
   $7,200 · 0%**, and **Choose Split It** goes to `plan_LiZXezzaPMzUF`. If Splitit
   was not requested, the Splitit block is absent.
10. Next steps is a green-outlined closed `<details>` under the payment buttons with
   **two paths**: Self Enroll (3 steps: welcome email login, Mark kickoff, Mastermind)
   and **5 Minute Call with CJ** (call/text). No two-email language. Opening it fires
   `next_steps_opened` once. It is never hidden behind checkout.
11. No All HTSA Resources tab, proof section, or CJ Reviews on close pages.

## Step 7 — ship it

Prefer `python3 scripts/htsa-paste-close.py --ship` so the BUYER swap, commit,
push, and live check happen in one shot. The script does not treat a cached old
invoice 200 as ready. It waits for this build's `close-build:` stamp. If the
clean URL is still stale it prints the same URL with `?v=<stamp>` so you can
send it immediately.

If you are already in the file by hand:

```bash
cd ~/Desktop/closewithcjclay.com/closewithcjclay.com
git add htsa-enrollment-<first>-<last>.html
git commit -m "Add close page for <Full Name>"
git push
```

Give CJ the live URL and tell him to load it once himself before the call.

## Step 8 — output EMAIL + TEXT every time

**Order is EMAIL first, then TEXT.** Send text immediately after email.
One enroll link only (in email body + optional duplicate at end of text).
The 30 day plan is already at the bottom of that page. Never write a
negative descriptive norm about other prospects.

**Fail-safe (generic) copy:** No first name. Email opens **Hi,** Text opens **Hey,**
Subject: **Your HTSA enrollment page is ready**. Link text:
**Click Here to Access Your HTSA Portal** → `https://closewithcjclay.com/access`.

**Personal copy (when CJ says personal / names the person):** Email opens
**Hi &lt;First&gt;,** Link text is exactly **`&lt;Full Name&gt; / Access`**
(clickable) pointing at their real
`https://closewithcjclay.com/htsa-enrollment-&lt;first&gt;-&lt;last&gt;.html`
URL. Never rename that URL. Never swap in `/access` for a named page. Put
`og:title` = `&lt;Full Name&gt; / Access` + `og:image` on their page so texts
show a preview card. Keep the body personal to what he said on the call.

